</computeroutput></literallayout></para>

<para><informaltable frame='bottom'><tgroup cols='1'><colspec align='center'/><tbody><row><entry align='center'>
</entry></row></tbody></tgroup></informaltable>
</para>
</section>
</section>
<section xml:id="_index_1autotoc_md41">
<title>Summary</title>
<para>Typical usage:</para>

<para><orderedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Initialize parser (<computeroutput><link linkend="_APC__ArgParser_8h_1a61d4424e1c28b49745d42226a00c60f4">apc_init</link></computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>Create argument definitions that can be modified (<computeroutput><link linkend="_APC__ArgParser_8h_1a89cd1dbd57bfa347f76c06add302ed98">apc_initInfo</link></computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>Register arguments (<computeroutput><link linkend="_APC__ArgParser_8h_1a249d5856e4d70717a20b468fd5600bbd">apc_add</link></computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>Query arguments (<computeroutput><link linkend="_APC__ArgParser_8h_1a00b47bfc8947418ae1f908f4de1f5f1e">apc_get</link></computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>Optionally generate help (<computeroutput><link linkend="_APC__ArgParser_8h_1a235f33a098769075131ad521168d2e0a">apc_generateHelp</link></computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>Destroy parser (<computeroutput><link linkend="_APC__ArgParser_8h_1acce093adeb486562d49b2e483102abbf">apc_destroy</link></computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>

<para>The API is intentionally minimal and explicit, designed to remain simple, predictable, and suitable for low-level C projects </para>
</section>
